      "problem": "A bank account had an **initial balance** of $$0.$ During the day, there was a **deposit** of $$20.$ Then there was a **withdrawal** of $$20$ later.\nWhat is the resulting amount in the account?",
      "worked_solution": "In our situation:\n\n- During the day, the account had a *deposit of* $$20,$ which is a change of $+$20.$\n\n- Later, the account had a *withdrawal of* $$20,$ which is a change of $-$20.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n20+(-20)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the balance returns to its original value of $$0.$",
